title: $:/plugins/rimir/work-focus/settings
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

\whitespace trim
\import $:/plugins/rimir/work-focus/engine $:/plugins/rimir/work-focus/edit-engine

\procedure wf-settings-area-edit()
<$transclude $variable="wf-area-open" area=<<area>>/>
\end

\procedure wf-settings-area-new()
<$transclude $variable="wf-area-new" tab={{{ [function[wf.active-tab]] }}}/>
<$action-setfield $tiddler="$:/temp/rimir/work-focus/open" text="yes"/>
<$action-setfield $tiddler="$:/temp/rimir/work-focus/edit" text="yes"/>
<$action-setfield $tiddler="$:/temp/rimir/work-focus/edit-view" text="areas"/>
\end

!! Work focus

A dock with attention counts and a drag action ring. See the <<tag "readme">> and documentation tabs. Areas, groups and actions are edited in the dock: open the panel and press ✎ (edit mode), or drag a row in edit mode and press ✎ on a tile. The buttons below open the same editors.

<table class="rr-table">
<tr><th>Setting</th><th>Value</th></tr>
<tr><td>Show the dock (`$:/config/rimir/work-focus/enabled`)</td><td><$checkbox tiddler="$:/config/rimir/work-focus/enabled" field="text" checked="yes" unchecked="no" default="yes"> enabled</$checkbox></td></tr>
<tr><td>Dock position (`.../position`): `top-left`, `top-right`, `bottom-left`, `bottom-right`</td><td><$select tiddler="$:/config/rimir/work-focus/position" default="top-left" class="rr-input"><option value="top-left">top-left</option><option value="top-right">top-right</option><option value="bottom-left">bottom-left</option><option value="bottom-right">bottom-right</option></$select></td></tr>
<tr><td>Date format written by actions (`.../date-format`), used when a date field is empty. Matches kind's date fields by default (`20261106`)</td><td><$edit-text tiddler="$:/config/rimir/work-focus/date-format" tag="input" class="rr-input" style="width:100%"/></td></tr>
<tr><td>Items shown per area before "+ N more" (`.../section-limit`)</td><td><$edit-text tiddler="$:/config/rimir/work-focus/section-limit" tag="input" class="rr-input" style="width:80px"/></td></tr>
</table>

The dock refreshes on reload, on ↻, after an action and when an edit is saved (closing an area card, leaving edit mode, the Save of a form). Changing a setting here shows at the next render; the area filters run at the next check.

!! Areas

Tiddlers tagged <<tag "$:/tags/rimir/work-focus/area">>, in tag order. The first area that matches an item claims it. A button opens the panel in edit mode on the area's tab with its card open (ring and panel: ✎ in the panel header).

<$list filter="[function[wf.areas]]" variable="a" emptyMessage="''None. Create one with + area.''">
<div class="wf-set-row"><$let area=<<a>>><$button class="tc-btn-invisible" actions=<<wf-settings-area-edit>> tooltip="Edit this area in the panel">✎&#32;<$text text={{{ [function[wf.caption],<a>] }}}/></$button></$let>&#32;<em><$text text={{{ [function[wf.level],<a>] }}}/></em>&#32;<code><$text text={{{ [<a>get[wf.filter]] }}}/></code></div>
</$list>

<$button actions=<<wf-settings-area-new>>>+ area</$button>

!! Groups

Ring groups, tagged <<tag "$:/tags/rimir/work-focus/group">>. A button opens the group form beside the dock. A group that came with the plugin can be overridden or hidden; "↺ Shipped" in the form restores it.

<$list filter="[function[wf.groups-all]]" variable="g">
<div class="wf-set-row"><$let kind="group" target=<<g>> item="" area="" preset="" side="right"><$button class="tc-btn-invisible" actions=<<wf-form-open>> tooltip="Edit this group">✎&#32;<$text text={{{ [function[wf.group-cap],<g>] }}}/></$button></$let>&#32;<code><$text text={{{ [<g>get[wf.name]] }}}/></code><$list filter="[<g>get[wf.hidden]match[yes]]" variable="x">&#32;<em>hidden</em></$list></div>
</$list>

<$let kind="group" target="" item="" area="" preset="" side="right"><$button actions=<<wf-form-open>>>+ group</$button></$let>

!! Actions

Ring tiles, tagged <<tag "$:/tags/rimir/work-focus/action">>. A button opens the action form.

<$list filter="[function[wf.actions-all]sort[caption]]" variable="a" emptyMessage="''None''">
<div class="wf-set-row"><$let kind="action" target=<<a>> item="" area="" preset="" side="right"><$button class="tc-btn-invisible" actions=<<wf-form-open>> tooltip="Edit this action">✎&#32;<$text text={{{ [<a>get[caption]] ~[<a>] }}}/></$button></$let>&#32;group&#32;<code><$text text={{{ [<a>get[wf.group]] }}}/></code>,&#32;recipe&#32;<code><$text text={{{ [<a>get[wf.recipe]] }}}/></code><$list filter="[<a>get[wf.hidden]match[yes]]" variable="x">&#32;<em>hidden</em></$list></div>
</$list>

<$let kind="action" target="" item="" area="" preset="" side="right"><$button actions=<<wf-form-open>>>+ action</$button></$let>

!! Recipes and info parts

Read-only. A recipe with a form (`<recipe>/form`) shows its settings in the action form; a bridge plugin adds one by shipping that tiddler.

<$list filter="[function[wf.recipes-all]]" variable="r">
<div class="wf-set-row">Recipe&#32;<code><$text text={{{ [<r>get[wf.name]] }}}/></code>:&#32;<$text text={{{ [<r>get[caption]] }}}/>&#32;<em><$text text={{{ [function[wf.recipe-form],<r>then[has a form]else[no form]] }}}/></em></div>
</$list>
<$list filter="[function[wf.tagged],[$:/tags/rimir/work-focus/info-part]]" variable="p">
<div class="wf-set-row">Info part&#32;<code><$text text={{{ [<p>get[wf.name]] }}}/></code>:&#32;<$text text={{{ [<p>get[caption]] }}}/></div>
</$list>
